2. GLOBAL (non-tool) RESULTS — type="error"
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Produced by the agent around any tool, never by the tool itself.

Unknown tool name:
    <tool_result type="error">unknown tool "foo"</result>

Extension/guard refusal (BeforeToolExecute):
    <tool_result type="error">tool call refused by extension guard</result>
    <tool_result type="error">THE REASON THE GUARD RETURNED</result>

Tool returned a Go error (any misuse: bad args, permission, not found…):
    <tool_result type="error">THE ERROR STRING (err.Error())</result>

Aborted turn (ctx cancelled / deadline):
    <tool_result type="error">aborted: context canceled</result>
    <tool_result type="error">aborted: context deadline exceeded</result>

Panic inside a tool (recovered):
    <tool_result type="error">panic: runtime error: index out of range [0] with length 0</result>

Interrupted turn (synthetic stub for a tool that never reported a result,
packages/core/message.go):
    <tool_result type="error">Tool outcome is unknown: execution may have occurred before interruption. Verify its effects or execution log before repeating a mutating action.</result>

Sandbox / jail refusals (returned as errors by the tools, sandbox.go):
    <tool_result type="error">jailed: path "/etc/passwd" is outside sandbox root "/home/u/proj" (use /unjail to disable)</result>
    <tool_result type="error">jailed: command contains banned pattern "rm -rf /" (use /unjail to disable)</result>
    <tool_result type="error">jailed: cd outside sandbox root is not allowed (use /unjail to disable)</result>

Permission refusals (returned as errors, permissions.go):
    <tool_result type="error">permission denied: this agent has no filesystem read permission</result>
    <tool_result type="error">permission denied: this agent has no filesystem write permission</result>
    <tool_result type="error">permission denied: this agent has no bash permission</result>
    <tool_result type="error">permission denied: filesystem read "/etc/passwd" is outside declared scopes</result>
    <tool_result type="error">permission denied: bash allowlist does not permit substitution or redirection</result>
